Recording the row and column additions, swaps and sign changes
gives unimodular ${\mathsf U},{\mathsf V}$ with
\[
 {\mathsf U}K{\mathsf V}=\operatorname{diag}(1,|P|).
\]
Each operation has its inverse of the same kind. For $P\ne0$
the isomorphism and inverse are
\[
 [y]\longmapsto ({\mathsf U}y)_2\bmod |P|,\qquad
 [1]\longmapsto[{\mathsf U}^{-1}(0,1)^t].
\]
Indeed ${\mathsf U}K=\operatorname{diag}(1,|P|){\mathsf V}^{-1}$, and a vector
${\mathsf U}y=(a,|P|b)^t$ comes from $K{\mathsf V}(a,b)^t$.

The exact old/new defect row now contains the complete final substitution; original before-text retained.
